alt:"Cartwheel showcase preview"},ue:["Gemini 2.5 Pro","Imagen 3"],modules:[{type:"hero",content:{date:"May 16, 2025",headline:"Cartwheel Advances Character Animation Using the Gemini API",Fe:[{name:"Jonathan Jarvis",role:"Co-founder & CTO"},{name:"Andrew Carr ",role:"Co-founder & Chief Scientist"},{name:"Vishal Dharmadhikari",role:"AI DevRel"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/Cartwheel_hero.jpg",type:"image",alt:"Cartwheel showcase hero"}}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-pro-latest"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Cartwheel advances character animation using the Gemini API</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Cartwheel stands at the forefront of next-generation animation, offering a platform where natural language inputs (e.g., "jump," "salsa dance spin") direct character actions. This innovation improves how creators animate for video, gaming, advertising, and social media. Cartwheel integrates Imagen 3 for intuitive text-to-character design, and harnesses Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview to develop sophisticated animation-specific algorithms, explore complex codebases, and accelerate platform optimization, empowering users to expand their creative storytelling.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Overcoming R&D hurdles in generative 3D motion</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              Developing a cutting-edge animation platform requires not only user-friendly design tools but also continuous innovation in backend algorithms and efficient codebase management. Cartwheel faced the challenge of rapidly prototyping and implementing complex animation features, optimizing their extensive codebase for performance, and enabling developers to quickly understand and contribute to a large-scale system. They needed a powerful AI partner to supercharge their development efforts.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>How Cartwheel uses Imagen 3 and Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              Cartwheel uses the Gemini API to improve its user-facing creation pipeline and to assist its internal development processes.\n            </p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>\n                <b>AI-Driven character conception with Imagen 3:</b> Cartwheel integrates Imagen 3 text-to-image capabilities, allowing creators to use text prompts to conceptualise and generate unique character visuals directly within the platform. These custom-designed characters can be animated using natural language, then exported fully rigged and ready for industry-standard 3D editing software like Maya or Blender, enabling integration into professional production environments.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                <b>Assisting R&D and optimization with Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview:</b> The Cartwheel team uses Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview internally to support its engineering and research workflows:\n                <ul>\n                  <li>\n                    <b>Developing algorithms:</b> Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview is employed to help develop animation-specific features, including algorithms for motion blur for data synthesis, Laplacian pyramids for blending, and auto IK (Inverse Kinematics) for in-editor posing.\n                  </li>\n                  <li>\n                    <b>Code exploration & debugging:</b> The team uses Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview to explore complex codebases, generate ideas for new experiments, and assist in efficiently debugging edge cases, such as intricate camera rotation errors.\n                  </li>\n                  <li>\n                    <b>Leveraging long context for codebase operations:</b> Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview\u2019s long context capabilities are used to operate over Cartwheel\u2019s entire codebase. This enables developers to, for example, bring new codebases (like the front-end) into context to help add features or ask high-level questions about the system\u2019s architecture and functionality.\n                  </li>\n                </ul>\n              </li>\n            </ul>"}},
{type:"youtube_video",content:{video:{kH:"2VxJBFecKkc"}}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Empowering animation workflows</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              By using Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview to assist with algorithm development, code exploration, and debugging, Cartwheel aims to enhance its development processes and accelerate platform optimisation. The integration of Imagen 3 provides users with a streamlined way to generate character visuals from text, while Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview serves as a tool to aid the developers building the underlying technology. These integrations support Cartwheel\u2019s goals of making animation workflows faster and more accessible, enabling uses like:\n            </p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>\n                Accelerating asset creation for games and video, allowing teams to focus on core design.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                Facilitating efficient marketing and social media content generation.\n              </li>\n            </ul>"}},
{type:"quote",content:{quote:"Animation is one of the purest ways to get a story out of your head and show it to the world. We\u2019re building tools to make that easier and more accessible for everyone!",author:"- Jonathan Jarvis, CEO / Co-founder, Cartwheel"}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Building the future of animation</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Cartwheel\u2019s integration of Imagen 3 and Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview highlights how Google AI can be applied to enable new user-facing features and assist the complex development work required to build next-generation tools.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Explore the <a href="https://cloud.google.com/gemini/docs/overview">Gemini API documentation</a>, learn about <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/image-generation#imagen">Imagen 3</a>, and get started in <a href="https://ai.dev">Google AI Studio</a>.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Cartwheel is a participant in <a href="https://labs.google/aifuturesfund">Google\u2019s AI Futures Fund</a> that invests in and collaborates with ambitious startups building what\u2019s next in AI.\n          </p>'}},
{type:"related_cases",content:{tf:["vela","joltai","optimalai"]}}]},{title:"Harvey",Xe:"Harvey uses its BigLaw Bench to demonstrate Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview's exceptional ability to handle complex legal reasoning tasks like due diligence and litigation drafting.",slug:"harvey",Cf:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-pro-latest",thumbnail:{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/Harvey_thumbnail.jpg",alt:"Harvey showcase preview"},ue:["Gemini 2.5 Pro"],modules:[{type:"hero",
content:{date:"May 16, 2025",headline:"Harvey: validating Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview\u2019s advanced legal reasoning with BigLaw Bench",Fe:[{name:"Niko Grupen",role:"Head of Applied AI"},{name:"Vishal Dharmadhikari",role:"AI DevRel"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/Harvey_hero.jpg",type:"image",alt:"Harvey showcase hero"}}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-pro-latest"}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Harvey: validating Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview\u2019s advanced legal reasoning with BigLaw Bench</h2>"},
body:"\n            <p>\n              The legal industry demands AI solutions that can navigate an immense volume of complex information with precision and nuance. Traditional AI benchmarks often fall short of capturing the real-world demands of legal practice, making it challenging to identify models truly capable of high-value legal work. Harvey, a dynamic startup dedicated to transforming legal workflows through AI, confronted this by developing BigLaw Bench, their comprehensive framework for assessing Large Language Model (LLM) performance on tasks mirroring actual legal work. In their recent rigorous evaluations, Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview emerged as a standout performer, demonstrating exceptional potential to improve efficiency in key legal domains.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview leads on BigLaw Bench</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              Harvey\u2019s recent evaluations leveraging the BigLaw Bench framework have clearly indicated that Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview demonstrates remarkable proficiency across core legal reasoning tasks and, in particular, tasks requiring reasoning over long-form legal inputs or outputs. As shown in Harvey\u2019s publicly shared results, obtained by testing models including Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview via their respective APIs, Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview achieved the leading score of 85.02% on BigLaw Bench, outperforming other models evaluated in this comprehensive assessment.\n            </p>\n          "}},
{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://ai.google.dev/static/images/showcase/harvey/harvey-graph.png",alt:'Bar chart titled "BigLaw Bench Score." Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview achieves the highest score of 85.02%.'}}]}},{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              This leading capability is crucial for a wide range of high-value legal activities. Key evaluation tasks within BigLaw Bench showcased Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview\u2019s strengths:\n            </p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>\n                <b>Transactional due diligence</b>: Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview showed a strong capacity to extract and summarize critical provisions (e.g., assignment, indemnification, termination clauses) from multiple lengthy service agreements. This suggests a significant potential to streamline the time-intensive process of manual document review.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                <b>Transaction structuring</b>: The model adeptly generated comprehensive, well-structured comparative analyses of intricate financial options (e.g., PIPE, underwritten equity offerings, bond offerings). The model showed promise in presenting this information in a clear and accessible manner, even for those without deep financial expertise, and in suggesting potential immediate action items.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                <b>Litigation drafting</b>: When assessed on tasks related to litigation, Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview exhibited a notable ability to generate detailed outlines for legal briefs based on substantial volumes of briefing documents. This capability points towards a future where AI can significantly aid in the initial stages of legal argument development and organization.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                <b>Document review & analysis</b>: Evaluations involving the review of disparate trial documents (call logs, emails, memoranda) revealed Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview\u2019s strength in creating coherent chronological summaries of events. Furthermore, the model showed potential in identifying critical inconsistencies and ambiguities within the record, a crucial aspect of thorough legal analysis.\n              </li>\n            </ul>\n            <p>\n              Across these evaluations, Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview showcased strong reasoning across inputs consisting of hundreds of pages of materials, a common scenario in legal work. In addition, it was capable of using these materials to generate longer-form and comprehensive outputs, allowing for deeper insights and analyses. These core capabilities highlight the potential for leveraging Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview across complex legal work requiring reasoning over large sets of documents to support diligence, review, and drafting use cases.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>A new standard for legal AI</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              "At Harvey, we\u2019re committed to equipping legal professionals with the most advanced tools," states Niko Grupen, Head of Applied AI at Harvey. "Our evaluation of Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview through BigLaw Bench has revealed its remarkable ability to synthesize complex legal information. This insight fuels our vision for future product development, where we aim to leverage these strengths to unlock unprecedented efficiency and empower lawyers to focus on higher-level strategic work."\n            </p>'}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Unlocking the future of legal work</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Harvey\u2019s commitment to rigorous evaluation and their insightful analysis of cutting-edge AI models like Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview are demonstrating the transformative potential of AI in the legal field. Their findings pave the way for future innovations that promise to reshape how legal professionals approach their most demanding tasks.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              To explore how Gemini 2.5 Pro Preview\u2019s advanced reasoning and synthesis capabilities can power your own applications, visit the <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs">Gemini API documentation</a> or get started in <a href="https://ai.dev">Google AI Studio</a>.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Harvey is a participant in <a href="https://labs.google/aifuturesfund">Google\u2019s AI Futures Fund</a> that invests in and collaborates with ambitious startups building what\u2019s next in AI.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"related_cases",content:{tf:["synthesia","toonsutra-2","volley-2"]}}]},{title:"Wolf Games",Xe:"Wolf Games uses Gemini API to boost content generation accuracy to 96% and slash latency to under 20 seconds for their daily crime stories.",slug:"wolfgames",Cf:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest",thumbnail:{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/Wolf_Games_thumbnail.jpg",alt:"Wolf Games showcase preview"},ue:["Gemini 2.0 Flash"],modules:[{type:"hero",
content:{date:"APRIL 9, 2025",headline:"How Wolf Games is crafting immersive crime stories daily with the Gemini API",Fe:[{name:"Noah Rosenberg",role:"Co-founder & CTO, Wolf Games"},{name:"Vishal Dharmadhikari",role:"Product Solutions Engineer"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/Wolf_Games_hero.jpg",type:"image",alt:"WolfGames showcase hero"}}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest"}},{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              The demand for fresh, engaging content in gaming is relentless. For Wolf Games, an innovative startup, this means delivering new, interactive crime stories to their players daily. They're achieving this ambitious goal by harnessing the power of the Gemini API, particularly Gemini 2.0 Flash and Gemini 2.0 Flash Thinking, to generate complex narratives at an unprecedented scale.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Wolf Games targets mobile gamers and mystery enthusiasts who crave daily problem-solving experiences. Their app delivers realistic crime scenes each day, complete with police reports, photos, interviews, and dynamic characters, allowing players to dive into new cold cases regularly.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>The challenge: scaling daily narrative content</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Maintaining this daily cadence requires speed and accuracy in content generation. Before integrating the Gemini API, Wolf Games faced hurdles with previous models that struggled with consistent structured output (achieving only 80% success) and slow prompt execution times (up to six minutes).\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              "We leverage the Gemini API within our prompt execution DAG to generate novel and engaging crime stories," explains Noah Rosenberg, Co-founder & CTO. "Our process orchestrates numerous finely-tuned prompts to yield structured content from an inherently unstructured process \u2013 narrative generation."\n            </p>'}},
{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://ai.google.dev/static/images/showcase/wolfgames/screenshot-1.png",alt:'Screenshot of a workflow application configuring an AI task named "Generate Synopsis" using the gemini/gemini-1.5-flash model.'}}]}},{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://ai.google.dev/static/images/showcase/wolfgames/screenshot-2.png",alt:'Screenshot of a workflow application configuring an AI task named "Generate Synopsis" using the gemini/gemini-1.5-flash model.'},
legend:'Screenshot of a workflow application configuring an AI task named "Generate Synopsis" using the gemini/gemini-1.5-flash model.'}]}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Wolf Games' innovative prompt engine</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              At the core of Wolf Games\' solution is their in-house tool, "Prompt Composer," which manages their prompt execution DAG. This framework allows them to integrate function calls, execute custom Python scripts for logic like ensuring unique  names, and manage state throughout the generation process. This allows them to:\n            </p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>\n                Easily switch between different models, including Gemini 2.5 Pro, Gemini 2.0 Flash and Gemini 2.0 Flash Thinking.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                Employ Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) by storing all generated content, such as character backstories and case events, in a persistent database, ensuring narrative cohesion. For instance, referencing a Bayesian causal graph of events, which maps out logical dependencies in the narrative, when generating a digital bank statement to ensure accuracy and consistency.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                Enforce structured output, particularly JSON, which is then validated using tools like Pydantic, ensuring reliability downstream.\n              </li>\n            </ul>\n            <p>\n              Wolf Games utilizes Gemini 2.0 Flash Thinking for complex text generation with large context windows (over 100k tokens) and outputs, consolidating workflows that previously required numerous steps. They find Gemini 2.0 Flash "incredibly performant and dependable" for faster tasks, often using Gemini 2.5 Pro to generate few-shot examples that enhance Gemini 2.0 Flash\'s performance.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              A key tool in their workflow is <a href="https://aistudio.google.com/">Google AI Studio</a>. "Google AI Studio has become my most frequently used Google product, surpassing even Gmail, Calendar, and Search in daily usage." shares Noah, highlighting its value for prompt experimentation.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Speed, accuracy, and an improved workflow</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Migrating to the Gemini models brought remarkable improvements:\n            </p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>\n                <strong>Increased accuracy</strong>: Prompt execution success rates soared from 80% to 96%, ensuring high-quality, structured content.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                <strong>Reduced latency</strong>: Prompt completion times dropped dramatically from minutes to under 20 seconds for most prompts.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                <strong>Streamlined content production</strong>: The speed and reliability of the Gemini models, especially Gemini 2.0 Flash, significantly enhanced their ability to produce detailed crime stories daily.\n              </li>\n            </ul>\n            <p>\n              "The Gemini models directly address our need for rapid and reliable generation of structured narrative content," Noah emphasizes. A critical threshold for Wolf Games is generating text faster than their writers can read it, maintaining their creative flow state \u2013 something the Gemini models have helped them consistently achieve.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Looking ahead</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Wolf Games plans to further leverage the Gemini API, particularly exploring the creative potential of upcoming models to generate even more realistic game evidence. Reflecting on their experience, Noah offers this advice to developers:\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              "Take the time to really understand how to structure prompts for the Gemini models. Use more powerful models to create the prompts for the faster models to execute." He stresses the importance of well-structured schema and few-shot examples, suggesting developers "run experiments to gain an intuition on how the Gemini models leverage the data encoded in the latent space."\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              For Noah, AI is a powerful creative catalyst: "I\u2019ve been a lifetime \'content klutz\'... Now with AI, I can create anything I can dream up, without all of the toil."\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Wolf Games\' innovative use of the Gemini API demonstrates its potential to revolutionize game development, enabling creators to produce immersive experiences at an unprecedented pace.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              You can get started in <a href="https://aistudio.google.com/">Google AI Studio</a> and <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api">explore the Gemini API documentation</a> to start building the future of AI.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"related_cases",content:{tf:["vela","joltai","optimalai"]}}]},{title:"Vela Partners",Xe:"Transforming VC with Gemini API: How Vela Partners Uses Grounding with Google Search for Deeper, Faster Insights",slug:"vela",Cf:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest",thumbnail:{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/Vela_Partners_thumbnail.jpg",alt:"Vela Partners showcase preview"},ue:["Gemini 2.0 Flash"],modules:[{type:"hero",content:{date:"APRIL 9, 2025",
headline:"Transforming VC with Gemini API: how Vela Partners uses grounding with Google search for deeper, faster insights",Fe:[{name:"Yigit Ihlamur",role:"General Partner and CTO"},{name:"Shrestha Basu Mallick",role:"Group Product Manager"},{name:"Vishal Dharmadhikari",role:"Product Solutions Engineer"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/Vela_Partners_hero.jpg",type:"image",alt:"AgentOps showcase hero"}}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest"}},
{type:"text",content:{body:'\n            <p>\n              In the high-stakes world of venture capital, identifying the most promising startups early on requires sifting through mountains of data and making swift, informed decisions. <a href="http://vela.partners/">Vela Partners</a>, a leading quant venture capital firm, is revolutionizing this process by leveraging the Gemini API, turning the art of investment into a data-driven science with unprecedented speed and precision.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Vela Partners isn\'t your typical VC. With a mission to be "100x faster and better," they\'ve embraced an AI-first strategy since 2017, investing exclusively in AI startups. To achieve this, they needed an AI platform that could keep pace. The Gemini API, particularly Gemini 2.0 Flash with Grounding with Google Search, provided the right solution.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://ai.google.dev/static/images/showcase/vela/vela-chat.png",alt:'Screenshot of the Vela search interface with the dropdown menu showing options to search across "Companies" or "People" databases.'}}]}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>How Vela Partners uses the Gemini API</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Vela Partners uses the Gemini API to power two critical workflows:\n            </p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>\n                <strong>Enriching startup profiles with Grounding</strong>: Early-stage startups, especially those born from open-source projects, often have minimal online presence. Vela uses Gemini 2.0 Flash grounded with Google Search to automatically fill in the gaps. When analyzing a GitHub repo, Gemini can surface key details about contributors \u2013 location, affiliations, experience \u2013 enriching the data used by Vela\'s internal models to assess potential. "Gemini and Grounding with Google Search has been exactly the solution that we were looking for a long while," says Zakari Salifu, AI Engineer at Vela Partners. This capability surpasses resource-intensive multi-agent frameworks and advanced analysis techniques (<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.19456">SSFF</a> and <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.12037#:~:text=This%20research%20introduces%20an%20innovative,ideas%20to%20enhance%20decision%2Dmaking">Founder-idea-fit</a>) previously explored by the firm.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                <strong>Streamlining due diligence with real-time analysis</strong>: Once a potential investment is identified, deep due diligence is crucial. The Gemini API, integrated via the Vercel AI SDK, pulls real-time data from news, social media, and more, providing a comprehensive view of the company and its market.\n              </li>\n            </ul>'}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>The \u201cmagic\u201d of grounding with Google search</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Before the Gemini API, gathering comprehensive information on nascent startups was a major bottleneck. "We invest in startups and people at their earliest stages," explains Yigit Ihlamur, General Partner and CTO. "At this stage, information is scattered across the web."\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              The Gemini API\'s Grounding with Google Search feature proved transformative. By grounding Gemini 2.0 Flash\'s responses in Google Search results, Vela significantly reduces the risk of hallucinations and ensures their analyses are based on the latest, most reliable public information. This was a game-changer compared to their previous in-house solutions.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Achieving speed, accuracy, and cost efficiency</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              For Vela, the Gemini API offered the ideal balance. While they had developed sophisticated proprietary methods, they sought a more efficient solution. Afriyie Samuel, Frontend Intelligence Engineer, notes, "We needed a lighter, more rapid, and cost-efficient version of deep company analysis. Gemini 2.0 Flash with Grounding has been exactly the solution we were looking for."\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Compared to other models, Gemini 2.0 Flash delivered superior performance for entity enrichment, even outperforming Vela\u2019s own internal techniques.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Expanding the AI frontier in venture capital</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Vela Partners is already seeing significant improvements in the speed and accuracy of their analyses. Looking forward, they plan to integrate the Gemini API further, exploring research features and file ingestion for due diligence.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Their advice to other developers? "Consider what Google is great at. Google is the undisputed leader in search technologies. Start using Gemini 2.0 Flash with grounded search and compare the quality of results with other LLMs out-of-the-box. You\u2019ll experience the magic."\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Vela Partners\' journey shows how the Gemini API is not just a tool, but a strategic advantage, empowering them to lead the way in the AI-driven future of venture capital.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Ready to build? <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api">Explore the Gemini API documentation</a>.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"related_cases",content:{tf:["wolfgames","joltai","langbase"]}}]},{title:"Jolt AI",Xe:"Jolt AI leverages the Gemini API to power its novel semantic search, enabling developers to instantly understand and navigate massive, 100k+ line codebases with significant improvements in speed, accuracy, and cost-effectiveness.",slug:"joltai",Cf:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest",thumbnail:{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/JoltAI_thumbnail.jpg",alt:"Jolt AI showcase preview"},
ue:["Gemini 2.0 Flash"],modules:[{type:"hero",content:{date:"APRIL 9, 2025",headline:"Scaling code understanding: how Jolt AI leverages the Gemini API",Fe:[{name:"Yev Spektor",role:"CEO"},{name:"Vishal Dharmadhikari",role:"Product Solutions Engineer"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/JoltAI_hero.jpg",type:"image",alt:"AgentOps showcase hero"}}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest"}},{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              Developers working with sprawling, production-scale codebases know the pain. Understanding context, finding relevant files, and making changes can feel like navigating a labyrinth. Jolt AI is tackling this head-on with a codegen and chat tool designed specifically for real-world, 100K+ line codebases. Their secret weapon for delivering both speed and accuracy? The Gemini API, particularly Gemini 2.0 Flash.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Jolt AI's mission is to enable developers to instantly understand and contribute to any codebase. Many of today's tools struggle with large, existing codebases and require users to manually select context files. It's tedious and impractical. Jolt AI uses a novel semantic search that accurately and automatically identifies the relevant context files. It's a game-changer for feature development, bug fixing, onboarding, and more.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://ai.google.dev/static/images/showcase/joltai/diagram-flow.png",alt:"Generated state flow diagram visualizing application logic."}}]}},{type:"text",content:{body:'\n            <p>\n              The challenge for Jolt AI was finding a model that could power their search pipeline with the right blend of speed, consistency, and code understanding. "We were looking to speed up 3 AI-backed steps in our code search pipeline," explains Yev Spektor, CEO of Jolt AI. "Each step requires an understanding of various programming languages, frameworks, user code, and user intent."\n            </p>'}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Gemini 2.0 Flash: delivering speed and enhanced code understanding</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Enter Gemini 2.0 Flash. For Jolt AI, this model delivered the performance leap they were seeking. "After some prompt tuning, we were able to get more consistent, higher-quality output with Gemini 2.0 Flash than we had with a slower, larger model from another provider," Spektor notes.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              How is Jolt AI using Gemini 2.0 Flash? It powers several crucial steps in their code search pipeline, providing the speed and accuracy needed to navigate and understand massive repositories. While the exact details are their "secret sauce," the impact is clear: Gemini 2.0 Flash enables Jolt AI to quickly surface the right information within complex codebases.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Switching to the Gemini API was remarkably efficient. "A couple hours to get the SDK implemented, and 2 days for prompt tuning and testing," reports Spektor. The team also utilized Google AI Studio for prompt ideation and tuning, streamlining the development process.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>The results: faster, higher quality, and more cost-effective</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              The move to Gemini 2.0 Flash has yielded impressive results for Jolt AI:\n            </p>\n            <ul>\n              <li>\n                <strong>70-80% Reduction in response times:</strong> The AI-backed steps in their search pipeline are significantly faster.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                <strong>Higher quality and more consistent answers:</strong> Users receive better results more than twice as fast.\n              </li>\n              <li>\n                <strong>80% Lower costs:</strong>  The migrated AI workloads are now significantly more cost-effective.\n              </li>\n            </ul>\n            <p>\n              "We are getting higher-quality answers to our users more than twice as quickly," Spektor emphasizes. This combination of speed, quality, and cost savings underscores the power of Gemini 2.0 Flash for performance-critical applications.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Future focus and developer insights</h2>"},body:'\n            <p>\n              Jolt AI is actively expanding its IDE support with an upcoming JetBrains plugin and exploring API accessibility. Spektor is excited about the broader potential of Jolt AI across enterprises, from aiding developers and engineering leaders to supporting customer support teams and enabling automated AI code pipelines.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Reflecting on their journey with the Gemini API, Spektor offers this advice to fellow developers:\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              "Gemini 2.0 Flash is more capable than you think, don\u2019t sleep on it. It\u2019s very good at recall - much better than some slow, more expensive models." He also encourages developers to explore the latest models from the Gemini family: "The new generation, Gemini 2.0 Flash and Gemini 2.5 Pro, need to be looked at. Gemini 2.0 Flash has made our product over twice as fast while increasing the quality of responses. The new models are a major step function."\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Jolt AI\'s success story highlights how the speed and capability of Gemini 2.0 Flash can significantly enhance AI-powered developer tools, especially those dealing with the complexities of large codebases.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Ready to build? Explore the <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api">Gemini API documentation</a> and get started with <a href="https://aistudio.google.com/">Google AI Studio</a> today.\n            </p>'}},
